-- Fixed and enhanced the issue of AI overbuilding defenders in the early game. It now tries (at least in theory in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` anyways etc) to replace the unit to build with an offense of versatile leaning. Typically, this means less longbowmen and more spearmen, camel archers, axemen, etc. We avoid to produce excess siege (in particular trebuchets-like units anyways etc) since they are not versatile enough to be used at defense and offense especially by the AI but anyways etc. The focus and assumption is we'll do good enough early where power differences are still not that great and gains potentially important to make. We also as of now favour civ-specific units (e.g. an egyptian war chariot rather than a horse archer if i'm not mistaken anyways etc) most times (except as of now e.g. counter units that are not especially favoured as they are less versatile or effective (e.g. maya holkan, etc), so prefer to produce a swordsman rather for example if i am not mistaken but anyways etc). If no good unit candidate is found, we attempt to hijack the unitai of the defensive unit (e.g. a longbowman with attack or attack_city or counter instead of city_defense). Results are very impressive!! They don't seem to always apply or entirely apply, but it does seem like most rivals have significantly less longbowmen and a more varied composition, and sometimes the difference is massive. For example in a run, hatshepsut ai went from +/- 30+ longbowmen for +/- 6 cities at turn 130 to 32 war chariots (plus camel archers for some reason etc), while some ais had often few, sometimes many longbowmen for some reason. Still, overall the seemingly more versatile compositions for all AI players, hopefully helps them better transition into an offensive middle game strategy and not be stuck with useless excess defenders. This should help boxed in players in particular, but also any AI with excess unit, after quite minimal defense needs are met (offense units can defend then as well and are more versatile if i am not mistaken but anyways etc, the varied composition also indirectly helps counter picks to invade us (like building spearmen vs chariots, or axes vs swords, hopefully, but anyways etc)). See originally changes in [53.2 - (Fixed and enhanced) Joao AI building way too many defenders (36 longbowmen at turn 130!! Almost all with UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE or similar) while being boxed in with only 3 cities, instead of making about half of these offense units or versatile ones to punish overextending thin neighbour, fixed by having an early phase "we have expectedly too few cities at this stage of the game, no need to overbuild anymore denders at this stage of the game, switch to offense or versatile UNITAI rather" and "our military composition has way too many defender UNITAIs, switch to offense or versatile UNITAIs", which seemingly fix the issue anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#532---fixed-and-enhanced-joao-ai-building-way-too-many-defenders-36-longbowmen-at-turn-130-almost-all-with-unitai_city_defense-or-similar-while-being-boxed-in-with-only-3-cities-instead-of-making-about-half-of-these-offense-units-or-versatile-ones-to-punish-overextending-thin-neighbour-fixed-by-having-an-early-phase-we-have-expectedly-too-few-cities-at-this-stage-of-the-game-no-need-to-overbuild-anymore-denders-at-this-stage-of-the-game-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitai-rather-and-our-military-composition-has-way-too-many-defender-unitais-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitais-which-seemingly-fix-the-issue-anyways-etc) and then a more refined and enhanced, as of now final version of these in [53.2.2 (Seemingly greatly enhanced) AI overproducing defenders early on, especially longbowmen but not only, replaced with an early produce more versatile units especially civ-specific ones when defended enough (at least in theory anyways etc) in CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#5322-seemingly-greatly-enhanced-ai-overproducing-defenders-early-on-especially-longbowmen-but-not-only-replaced-with-an-early-produce-more-versatile-units-especially-civ-specific-ones-when-defended-enough-at-least-in-theory-anyways-etc-in-cvcityaiai_chooseunit-anyways-etc) anyways etc.
